From e34cf8821d46d35fd0515028ea28fbf816969881 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:25:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] feat(edm): wire EDM constant taper - posed moves,
 leaning-kerf verify, max-angle and U/V refusals

A Wire Contour states a signed taper angle (#290 D2): the profile and
the #532 laws hold on the top plane at the kerf across the leaning
wire, each side leans square to itself and the corners along the
mitre, and every move's pose is the wire's direction toward the upper
guide. The wire laws (#534) read a stated taper's poses as the wire's
lean at every judged height (elliptical kerf reach), so a gouge at any
height blocks the post; any other posed move stays refused. The
machine check judges every lean against edm.max_taper_deg, the guide
planes and the U/V strokes; the wire post writes taper_on / uv /
taper_off from edm.codes with X Y at the lower guide. Zero taper is
byte-identical to the vertical cut.

Fixes #536

